{% from "govuk/components/button/macro.njk" import govukButton %}

{# RA-335. Case-panel affordances (reassign, unassign, change/override due
   date, query, withdraw, approve, create work item) navigate to another
   page rather than submitting a form — some rendered as plain text links,
   others (approve, create work item) as button-styled links via
   govukButton's `href` param. Neither has a native disabled state: an
   anchor has none at all, and govukButton silently ignores `disabled` the
   moment `href` is set (it only ever applies to a real `<button>`). This
   site also renders no JavaScript to intercept a click (RA-94), so for a
   read-only support user the affordance is rendered as an inert `<span>`
   instead — no `href` at all, so there is nothing to navigate to and
   nothing for a keyboard or screen-reader user to activate.

   `variant` picks the enabled-state markup:
   - 'link' (default): a plain `<a class="{{ classes }}" href="...">`.
     `classes` here is the FULL class string (e.g. "govuk-link").
   - 'button': delegates the enabled state to the real `govukButton`
     macro, so it keeps govuk-frontend's own `role="button"`,
     `data-module="govuk-button"` and `draggable="false"` on the anchor
     — a hand-rolled `<a>` regresses keyboard (space-bar activation)
     and screen-reader support, since those only apply via
     govuk-frontend's own template. `classes` here is the EXTRA class
     string only (govukButton always prepends its own "govuk-button"
     class).

   Either way, when disabled, the class string used for the span is
   built the same way govuk-frontend would have built it, so the
   disabled state keeps the same visual shape as the enabled one. #}
{% macro appActionLink(params) %}
  {% if params.disabled %}
    {% set disabledClasses = ('govuk-button ' if params.variant == 'button') + params.classes + ' app-action-link--disabled' %}
    <span class="{{ disabledClasses }}" aria-disabled="true"{% if params.testId %} data-testid="{{ params.testId }}"{% endif %}>{{ params.text }}</span>
  {% elif params.variant == 'button' %}
    {{ govukButton({
      text: params.text,
      href: params.href,
      classes: params.classes,
      attributes: { "data-testid": params.testId } if params.testId else {}
    }) }}
  {% else %}
    <a class="{{ params.classes }}" href="{{ params.href }}"{% if params.testId %} data-testid="{{ params.testId }}"{% endif %}>{{ params.text }}</a>
  {% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
